//
// Flist.g6lc — brand-forward manifest alias for GSys LibreCore.
//
// This is an ALIAS, not a fork. It exists so that integration scripts, SoC
// flists and downstream projects can reference the LibreCore name without this
// project having to rename `core/Flist.cva6` — a file owned by the OpenHW Group
// (Solderpad SHL-2.0) whose renaming would break upstream rebase for zero
// benefit. See AGENTS-branding.md §3 ("rename at the boundary, never inside").
//
// Contents are therefore exactly Flist.cva6 plus the LibreCore naming seam.
//
// USAGE
//   -f ${CVA6_REPO_DIR}/core/Flist.g6lc
//
// NOTE ON THE TOP MODULE
//   The elaboration top is still `cva6` (core/cva6.sv, tier U / OpenHW).
//   A branded `g6lc` top wrapper is deliberately NOT provided yet: cva6.sv's
//   declaration is 362 lines with 31 parameter lines including inline
//   `parameter type ... struct packed` injections, and a hand-transcribed
//   wrapper cannot be validated without a Verilator elaboration gate
//   (AGENTS.md §0.2). Tracked in AGENTS-todo.md as a release blocker.
//
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

// The LibreCore naming seam (g6lc_cfg_t alias + brand identity constants).
// Must be compiled after config_pkg, which Flist.cva6 provides.
-f ${CVA6_REPO_DIR}/core/Flist.cva6

${CVA6_REPO_DIR}/core/include/g6lc_pkg.sv

// end of manifest
